{"id":"G0782","lemma":"ἀσπάζομαι","transliteration":"aspazomai","sayIt":"aspazomai","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to pay respects to","meaning":"ἀσπάζομαι depon.,\n[in LXX: Eze.18:7, Jdg.18:15 (שָׁלוֹם שָׁאַל), Est.5:2, 1Ma.7:29, al. ;]\nto welcome, greet, salute: with accusative of person(s), Mat.5:47, Mrk.9:15, Act.21:7, al.; id. before ἐν φιλήματι, Rom.16:16, 1Co.16:20, 2Co.13:12, 1Th.5:26, 1Pe.5:14; τ. ἐκκλησίαν (Deiss., BS, 257), Act.18:22; as term. tech. for conveying greetings at the end of a letter (MM, see word), used by an amanuensis (Milligan, NTD, 23), Rom.16:22 (on the aoristic Pres., here and elsewhere, see M, Pr., 119; Bl., § 56, 4); κατήντησαν . . . ἀσπασάμενοι (on this constr., see El., § 58, 4; M, Pr., 132, 238), Act.25:13 (cf. ἀπ-ἀπ-ασπάζομαι).†\n(AS)","glosses":["greet","sends you greetings","send you greetings","greeted","salute","do not greet"],"count":47,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":47,"renderings":{"bsb":"you greet","kjv":"ye salute"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"greet","kjv":"salute"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-9","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"to greet","kjv":"him saluted"}},{"chapterId":"mrk-15","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"to salute","kjv":"to salute"}},{"chapterId":"luk-1","v":40,"renderings":{"bsb":"greeted","kjv":"saluted"}},{"chapterId":"luk-10","v":4,"renderings":{"bsb":"Do not greet","kjv":"salute"}},{"chapterId":"act-18","v":22,"renderings":{"bsb":"greeted","kjv":"saluted"}},{"chapterId":"act-20","v":1,"renderings":{"bsb":"he said goodbye to them","kjv":"embraced"}},{"chapterId":"act-21","v":6,"renderings":{"kjv":"when we had taken our leave"}},{"chapterId":"act-21","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"we greeted","kjv":"saluted"}},{"chapterId":"act-21","v":19,"renderings":{"bsb":"Paul greeted","kjv":"when he had saluted"}},{"chapterId":"act-25","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"to pay their respects","kjv":"to salute"}},{"chapterId":"rom-16","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"Greet","kjv":"Greet"}},{"chapterId":"r